# Static-analysis policy for the Qt test translation units.
#
# Inherits the repository policy and removes one check that cannot be satisfied
# here. A Qt test case is a private slot invoked through the meta-object system,
# which cannot invoke a static member function. Converting one as suggested
# removes the case from the run while leaving the file compiling and the suite
# green, so the advice is not merely noisy here but actively unsafe.
#
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity is removed for a different reason.
# The metric measures branching and nesting, and a test function is supposed to
# be a long straight line of arrange, act, and assert; scoring one says nothing
# about whether the code under test is hard to follow, which is the only
# question the check was added to answer. Sixty-seven of its seventy-four
# occurrences across the tree were test functions, and they were the reason the
# seven that name real project code were hard to see at all.
#
# Both exclusions are scoped to this directory. The same checks stay enabled for
# application and core sources, where their advice is sound.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
